    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d458">

                <pb facs="0547" n="435" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg435"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.01/142: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-27T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 27,
                                1919, 7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3270. For Polk.</p>
                <p>Your 4370, September 26, midnight.</p>
                <p>No change in policy. We are not withdrawing support of Kolchak. On the contrary we are continuing to
                    ship rifles and President has just approved application of Russian Ambassador to
                    buy on a credit basis surplus cloth and clothing for Kolchak forces. After submitting question to
                    the President we have also approved purchase by Kolchak Government of Russian rouble notes<anchor n="73"
                        xml:id="d458-f1"/> concerning which you will recall much discussion in the
                    past. I am taking up with President question of Kolchak’s recognition.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d458-f1" n="73" xml:id="d458-f1-content">
                <p>See section on Release to the Kolchak
                    Government of the Russian State Bank Notes Printed in the United States, <ref
                        target="#pg453">pp. 453</ref> ff.; see also <ref
                        target="frus1918Russiav03#pg_72"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1918, Russia, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>,
                        pp. 72</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
